      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<hr><br><strong>EDOS Label</strong><br><p>1.1 threats of harm – Expressing intent, willingness or desire to harm an individual woman or group of women. This could include, but is not limited to: physical, sexual, emotional or privacy-based forms of harm.</p><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Cyber harassment includes threats of physical and/or sexual violence delivered by email, text, or online message. It also includes hate speech, meaning language that denigrates, insults, threatens, or targets an individual because of her gender and other traits. These threats can involve use of force through threats or abuse of vulnerability, power, or trust, and can be perpetrated by someone in the intimate sphere, including a spouse, partner, former partner, family member, or someone within the domestic unit or home.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the description of the EDOS label?</strong>",
        "DefaultChoices": false,
