      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<hr><br><strong>EDOS Label</strong><br><p>1.1 threats of harm – Expressing intent, willingness or desire to harm an individual woman or group of women. This could include, but is not limited to: physical, sexual, emotional or privacy-based forms of harm.</p><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Online mob attacks against women include often-credible rape and death threats, with real-life targeting adding to their credibility. These attacks span multiple platforms and involve intense, sustained threats from many attackers in concerted and often coordinated campaigns. Violent mobs threaten and target women with sexual violence, especially women with intersecting vulnerabilities, and crowds play a role in destroying privacy.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the description of the EDOS label?</strong>",
