      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<hr><br><strong>EDOS Label</strong><br><p>1.2 incitement and encouragement of harm – Inciting or encouraging an individual, group, or general audience to harm a woman or group of women. It includes language where the author seeks to rationalise and/or justify harming women to another person.</p><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Online gender-based hate speech includes content that spreads, incites, promotes, or justifies hatred against women and girls based on gender or gender combined with other characteristics. It can include violent content portraying women and girls as sexual objects or targets of violence, shared privately or publicly and often directed at women in public-facing roles. Acts of abuse can start online and continue offline, or start offline and continue online.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the description of the EDOS label?</strong>",
