      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<hr><br><strong>EDOS Label</strong><br><p>1.2 incitement and encouragement of harm – Inciting or encouraging an individual, group, or general audience to harm a woman or group of women. It includes language where the author seeks to rationalise and/or justify harming women to another person.</p><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Sexist hate speech is defined as expressions that spread, incite, promote, or justify hatred based on sex. Posting and sharing violent content involves portraying women as sexual objects or as targets of violence. Sexist and insulting comments are used to abuse women for expressing their own views and for turning away sexual advances.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the description of the EDOS label?</strong>",
