    {
      "SurveyID": "SV_9Kzg3KA9F3QnEFM",
      "Element": "SQ",
      "PrimaryAttribute": "QID64",
      "SecondaryAttribute": "answer_relevance_card_ff7874374b5a86fe7bfdbe1c__deepseek_deepseek-v4_1-flash-1017",
      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<hr><br><strong>EDOS Label</strong><br><p>1.2 incitement and encouragement of harm – Inciting or encouraging an individual, group, or general audience to harm a woman or group of women. It includes language where the author seeks to rationalise and/or justify harming women to another person.</p><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Sexist hate speech includes expressions that spread, incite, promote, or justify hatred based on sex. Its forms include brutal and sexualised threats of death, rape, and violence, as well as victim blaming and re-victimisation, which can shift blame onto targeted women. It can also use humour, false compliments, or supposed jokes to humiliate and ridicule the target.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the description of the EDOS label?</strong>",
        "DefaultChoices": false,
