      "SurveyID": "SV_9Kzg3KA9F3QnEFM",
      "Element": "SQ",
      "PrimaryAttribute": "QID83",
      "SecondaryAttribute": "faithfulness_card_13d1cb3d472cecc410555c51__openai_gpt-6_1-sol",
      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<strong>Paragraph</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Impact of sexist hate speech on women and girls\n\nSexist hate speech is often treated as a harmless and non-serious issue and women are explicitly or implicitly told to bear with it. However, not only does sexist hate speech undermine freedom of speech for women and girls, but its psychological, emotional and/or physical impacts are real and severe. The aim of sexist hate speech is to humiliate or objectify women, to undervalue their skills and opinions, to destroy their reputation, to make them feel vulnerable and fearful, and to control and punish them for not following a certain behaviour. Sexist hate speech has the effect of silencing women, obliging them to adapt their behaviour and limit their movements and participation in diverse human activities.</div><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Sexist hate speech aims to humiliate or objectify women, devalue their skills and opinions, damage their reputations, instill vulnerability and fear, and control or punish departures from expected behaviour. Its psychological, emotional and/or physical impacts are real and severe, despite being treated as harmless or something women should endure. It undermines women’s and girls’ freedom of speech, silencing women and obliging them to adapt their behaviour and limit their movements and participation in diverse activities.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the paragraph?</strong>",
        "DefaultChoices": false,
        "DataExportTag": "faithfulness_card_13d1cb3d472cecc410555c51__openai_gpt-6_1-sol",
