    {
      "SurveyID": "SV_9Kzg3KA9F3QnEFM",
      "Element": "SQ",
      "PrimaryAttribute": "QID84",
      "SecondaryAttribute": "answer_relevance_card_13d1cb3d472cecc410555c51__openai_gpt-6_1-sol",
      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<hr><br><strong>EDOS Label</strong><br><p>2.2 aggressive and emotive attacks – Expressing strong negative sentiment against women, such as disgust or hatred. This can be through direct description of the speaker’s subjective emotions, baseless accusations, or the use of gendered slurs, gender-based profanities and gender-based insults.</p><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Sexist hate speech aims to humiliate or objectify women, devalue their skills and opinions, damage their reputations, instill vulnerability and fear, and control or punish departures from expected behaviour. Its psychological, emotional and/or physical impacts are real and severe, despite being treated as harmless or something women should endure. It undermines women’s and girls’ freedom of speech, silencing women and obliging them to adapt their behaviour and limit their movements and participation in diverse activities.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the description of the EDOS label?</strong>",
        "DefaultChoices": false,
