      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<hr><br><strong>EDOS Label</strong><br><p>2.2 aggressive and emotive attacks – Expressing strong negative sentiment against women, such as disgust or hatred. This can be through direct description of the speaker’s subjective emotions, baseless accusations, or the use of gendered slurs, gender-based profanities and gender-based insults.</p><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Flaming is aggressive, hostile online communication characterised by insults, negative emotion, and emphatic typography such as capital letters and exclamation marks. It deliberately uses swearing or offensive language to express emotionally charged or contrarian statements, usually to provoke a response from another user. Flaming can be openly misogynous and is often directed at women through threats or fantasies of sexual violence, or incitement to sexual violence.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the description of the EDOS label?</strong>",
        "DefaultChoices": false,
