    {
      "SurveyID": "SV_9Kzg3KA9F3QnEFM",
      "Element": "SQ",
      "PrimaryAttribute": "QID91",
      "SecondaryAttribute": "faithfulness_card_49ec5cc0bc81537b665dab31__deepseek_deepseek-v4_1-flash-1017",
      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<strong>Paragraph</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Impact of sexist hate speech on women and girls\n\nSexist hate speech is often treated as a harmless and non-serious issue and women are explicitly or implicitly told to bear with it. However, not only does sexist hate speech undermine freedom of speech for women and girls, but its psychological, emotional and/or physical impacts are real and severe. The aim of sexist hate speech is to humiliate or objectify women, to undervalue their skills and opinions, to destroy their reputation, to make them feel vulnerable and fearful, and to control and punish them for not following a certain behaviour. Sexist hate speech has the effect of silencing women, obliging them to adapt their behaviour and limit their movements and participation in diverse human activities.</div><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Sexist hate speech is often dismissed as harmless, and women are explicitly or implicitly told to bear with it, even though its psychological, emotional, and physical impacts are severe. Its aims include humiliating or objectifying women, undervaluing their skills and opinions, destroying their reputation, making them feel vulnerable and fearful, and controlling or punishing them for not conforming to expected behavior. It has the effect of silencing women and obliging them to adapt their behavior and limit their movements and participation in diverse activities.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the paragraph?</strong>",
        "DefaultChoices": false,
        "DataExportTag": "faithfulness_card_49ec5cc0bc81537b665dab31__deepseek_deepseek-v4_1-flash-1017",
        "QuestionType": "MC",
        "Selector": "SAVR",
        "SubSelector": "TX",
