        "QuestionText": "<hr><br><strong>EDOS Label</strong><br><p>2.2 aggressive and emotive attacks – Expressing strong negative sentiment against women, such as disgust or hatred. This can be through direct description of the speaker’s subjective emotions, baseless accusations, or the use of gendered slurs, gender-based profanities and gender-based insults.</p><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Online gender-based hate speech is content posted and shared through ICT means that is hateful toward women and/or girls because of their gender or because of a combination of gender and other factors such as race, age, disability, sexuality, ethnicity, nationality, religion or profession. It also includes content that spreads, incites, promotes or justifies hatred based on gender or on a combination of gender and other factors. Such content can portray women and girls as sexual objects or targets of violence and is often targeted at women in public-facing roles. These acts can start online and continue offline, start offline and continue online, and can be perpetrated by unknown persons or groups as well as by persons or groups known to the victim.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the description of the EDOS label?</strong>",
