      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<hr><br><strong>EDOS Label</strong><br><p>2.3 dehumanising attacks and overt sexual objectification – Derogating women by comparing them to non-human entities such as vermin, disease or refuse, or overtly reducing them to sexual objects.</p><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Sexist hate speech can express contempt toward a person or treat them as inferior or essentially reduced to their sexual dimension. Online and offline forms include slut-shaming, body-shaming, non-consensual sharing of sexual images, sexualised threats of rape and violence, and offensive comments about appearance, sexuality, sexual orientation, or gender roles; supposed jokes and false compliments can be used to humiliate and ridicule targets. Many targeted women do not report sexist hate speech, so its true extent remains partly hidden.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the description of the EDOS label?</strong>",
        "DefaultChoices": false,
        "DataExportTag": "answer_relevance_card_b81e33f93f1037b909900394__deepseek_deepseek-v4_1-flash-1017",
