    {
      "SurveyID": "SV_9Kzg3KA9F3QnEFM",
      "Element": "SQ",
      "PrimaryAttribute": "QID103",
      "SecondaryAttribute": "faithfulness_card_f8d7f4cebfb8b3876317dfcd__deepseek_deepseek-v4_1-flash-1017",
      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<strong>Paragraph</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">4. Towards common definitions of cyber violence against women and girls &gt; Proposed definition\n\nattacks perpetrated against more vulnerable groups of women and girls (including journal- ists, politicians, activists, LGBTIQ+, etc.) are detected and more insights are gained into the phenomenon.\n\nOnline gender-based hate speech is defined as content posted and shared through ICT means that:\n\nis hateful towards women and/or girls because of their gender, or because of a combination of gender and other factors (e.g. race, age, disability, sexuality, ethnicity, nationality, religion or profession); and/or\n\nspreads, incites, promotes or justifies hatred based on gender, or because of a combi- nation of gender and other factors (e.g. race, age, disability, sexuality, ethnicity, nationality, religion or profession).\n\nIt can also involve posting and sharing, through ICT means, violent content that consists of portraying women and girls as sexual objects or targets of violence. This content can be sent privately or publicly and is often targeted at women in public-facing roles.\n\nThe acts can:\n\na. start online and continue offline;\n\nb. start offline and continue online;\n\nc. can be perpetrated by an unknown person / group of people who are unknown to the victim; or\n\nd. can be perpetrated by a person or/ group of people who are known to the victim.</div><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Online gender-based hate speech includes content posted and shared through ICT means that is hateful toward women and/or girls because of gender or combined gender and other factors, and content that spreads, incites, promotes, or justifies hatred on those bases. It can also involve violent content portraying women and girls as sexual objects or targets of violence. This content can be sent privately or publicly and is often targeted at women in public-facing roles. Such acts may begin online and continue offline, begin offline and continue online, and may be perpetrated by unknown people or by people known to the victim.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the paragraph?</strong>",
        "DefaultChoices": false,
        "DataExportTag": "faithfulness_card_f8d7f4cebfb8b3876317dfcd__deepseek_deepseek-v4_1-flash-1017",
