        "QuestionText": "<hr><br><strong>EDOS Label</strong><br><p>2.3 dehumanising attacks and overt sexual objectification – Derogating women by comparing them to non-human entities such as vermin, disease or refuse, or overtly reducing them to sexual objects.</p><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Online gender-based hate speech includes content posted and shared through ICT means that is hateful toward women and/or girls because of gender or combined gender and other factors, and content that spreads, incites, promotes, or justifies hatred on those bases. It can also involve violent content portraying women and girls as sexual objects or targets of violence. This content can be sent privately or publicly and is often targeted at women in public-facing roles. Such acts may begin online and continue offline, begin offline and continue online, and may be perpetrated by unknown people or by people known to the victim.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the description of the EDOS label?</strong>",
