      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<hr><br><strong>EDOS Label</strong><br><p>3.1 casual use of gendered slurs, profanities, and insults – Using gendered slurs, gender-based profanities and insults, but not to intentionally attack women. Only terms that traditionally describe women are in scope (e.g. ‘b*tch’, ‘sl*t’).</p><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Components of online gender-based hate speech include abusive or insulting words and written material, conduct that spreads sexism, and comments or behaviour with sexual or sexist connotations. Associated effects include reputational harm, loss of confidence, and the creation of an intimidating, hostile or offensive situation. The information does not distinguish casual uses of gendered insults from intentional attacks.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the description of the EDOS label?</strong>",
