        "QuestionText": "<hr><br><strong>EDOS Label</strong><br><p>3.1 casual use of gendered slurs, profanities, and insults – Using gendered slurs, gender-based profanities and insults, but not to intentionally attack women. Only terms that traditionally describe women are in scope (e.g. ‘b*tch’, ‘sl*t’).</p><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Avoiding sexist language online is part of taking personal responsibility for ending online gender-based violence. Men and boys can educate themselves and others by learning about its nature, extent, and impact, sharing resources, participating in awareness campaigns, and discussing respectful online behaviour.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the description of the EDOS label?</strong>",
