    {
      "SurveyID": "SV_9Kzg3KA9F3QnEFM",
      "Element": "SQ",
      "PrimaryAttribute": "QID136",
      "SecondaryAttribute": "answer_relevance_card_9ce173f8f827c4a78c372ada__deepseek_deepseek-v4_1-flash-1017",
      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<hr><br><strong>EDOS Label</strong><br><p>3.2 immutable gender differences and gender stereotypes – Asserting immutable, natural or otherwise essential differences between men and women. In some cases, this could be in the form of using women’s traits to attack men. Most sexist jokes will fall into this category.</p><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Sexist hate speech can express contempt toward a person based on sex or gender and can treat that person as inferior or essentially reduced to their sexual dimension. It includes offensive comments on appearance, sexuality, sexual orientation, or gender roles, as well as false compliments or supposed jokes that use humour to humiliate and ridicule the target. Many targeted women do not report sexist hate speech, which partly hides its extent.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the description of the EDOS label?</strong>",
        "DefaultChoices": false,
        "DataExportTag": "answer_relevance_card_9ce173f8f827c4a78c372ada__deepseek_deepseek-v4_1-flash-1017",
