      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<strong>Paragraph</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Appendix to Recommendation CM/Rec(2019)1 &gt; Guidelines for preventing and combating sexism: measures for implementation &gt; Context\n\n2. “Gender stereotypes are preconceived social and cultural patterns or ideas whereby women and men are assigned characteristics and roles determined and limited by their sex. Gender stereotyping presents a serious obstacle to the achievement of real gender equality and feeds into gender discrimination. Such stereotyping can limit the development of the natural talents and abilities of girls and boys, women and men, their educational and professional preferences and experiences, as well as life opportunities in general.” (Council of Europe Gender Equality Strategy 2018-2023, Strategic objective 1)\n\nSexism and sexist behaviour result in physical, sexual, psychological or socio-economic harm and impact different sectors of the population differently. Women and girls are disproportionately affected by such behaviour. Sexism and sexist behaviour constitute a barrier to the empowerment and advancement of women and girls; the elimination of sexism and sexist behaviour would benefit everyone: women, girls, men and boys.</div><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Gender stereotypes are preconceived social and cultural patterns or ideas that assign women and men characteristics and roles determined and limited by their sex. Such stereotyping is a serious obstacle to gender equality and feeds into gender discrimination. It can limit the development of girls’ and boys’, women’s and men’s natural talents and abilities, their educational and professional preferences and experiences, and their life opportunities in general. Sexism and sexist behaviour cause physical, sexual, psychological or socio-economic harm, disproportionately affect women and girls, and constitute a barrier to women’s and girls’ empowerment and advancement.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the paragraph?</strong>",
        "DefaultChoices": false,
        "DataExportTag": "faithfulness_card_c6e67aff27968f7f4ca279ed__deepseek_deepseek-v4_1-flash-1017",
