      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<hr><br><strong>EDOS Label</strong><br><p>3.2 immutable gender differences and gender stereotypes – Asserting immutable, natural or otherwise essential differences between men and women. In some cases, this could be in the form of using women’s traits to attack men. Most sexist jokes will fall into this category.</p><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Gender stereotypes are preconceived social and cultural patterns or ideas that assign women and men characteristics and roles determined and limited by their sex. Such stereotyping is a serious obstacle to gender equality and feeds into gender discrimination. It can limit the development of girls’ and boys’, women’s and men’s natural talents and abilities, their educational and professional preferences and experiences, and their life opportunities in general. Sexism and sexist behaviour cause physical, sexual, psychological or socio-economic harm, disproportionately affect women and girls, and constitute a barrier to women’s and girls’ empowerment and advancement.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the description of the EDOS label?</strong>",
        "DefaultChoices": false,
        "DataExportTag": "answer_relevance_card_c6e67aff27968f7f4ca279ed__deepseek_deepseek-v4_1-flash-1017",
