      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<hr><br><strong>EDOS Label</strong><br><p>3.4 condescending explanations or unwelcome advice – Offering unsolicited or patronising advice to women on topics and issues they know more about (known as ‘mansplaining’).</p><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Sexism includes any act, gesture, visual representation, spoken or written words, practice, or behaviour based on the idea that a person or group is inferior because of sex, whether online or offline and in public or private. Such conduct is sexist when it has the purpose or effect of violating dignity or rights, causing physical, sexual, psychological, or socio-economic harm, creating an intimidating, hostile, degrading, humiliating, or offensive environment, constituting a barrier to autonomy and full realisation of human rights, or maintaining and reinforcing gender stereotypes.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the description of the EDOS label?</strong>",
