    {
      "SurveyID": "SV_9Kzg3KA9F3QnEFM",
      "Element": "SQ",
      "PrimaryAttribute": "QID171",
      "SecondaryAttribute": "faithfulness_card_d1c2da456cd10f65596b9032__deepseek_deepseek-v4_1-flash-1017",
      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<strong>Paragraph</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">CM/Rec(2019)1<sup>1</sup>\n\nAffirming that sexism is reinforced by gender stereotypes affecting women and men, girls and boys, and runs counter to achieving gender equality and inclusive societies;\n\nNoting that sexism constitutes a barrier to the empowerment of women and girls, who are disproportionately affected by sexist behaviour; and further noting that gender stereotypes and inherent biases shape the norms, behaviour and expectations of men and boys, and therefore lead to sexist acts;\n\nConcerned that sexism is linked to violence against women and girls, whereby acts of “everyday” sexism are part of a continuum of violence creating a climate of intimidation, fear, discrimination, exclusion and insecurity which limits opportunities and freedom;</div><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Sexism is reinforced by gender stereotypes and inherent biases that shape the norms, behaviour and expectations of men and boys and lead to sexist acts. Acts of “everyday” sexism are part of a continuum of violence against women and girls that creates a climate of intimidation, fear, discrimination, exclusion and insecurity. This climate limits women’s and girls’ opportunities and freedom and acts as a barrier to their empowerment.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the paragraph?</strong>",
        "DefaultChoices": false,
        "DataExportTag": "faithfulness_card_d1c2da456cd10f65596b9032__deepseek_deepseek-v4_1-flash-1017",
        "QuestionType": "MC",
