    {
      "SurveyID": "SV_9Kzg3KA9F3QnEFM",
      "Element": "SQ",
      "PrimaryAttribute": "QID172",
      "SecondaryAttribute": "answer_relevance_card_d1c2da456cd10f65596b9032__deepseek_deepseek-v4_1-flash-1017",
      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<hr><br><strong>EDOS Label</strong><br><p>3.4 condescending explanations or unwelcome advice – Offering unsolicited or patronising advice to women on topics and issues they know more about (known as ‘mansplaining’).</p><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Sexism is reinforced by gender stereotypes and inherent biases that shape the norms, behaviour and expectations of men and boys and lead to sexist acts. Acts of “everyday” sexism are part of a continuum of violence against women and girls that creates a climate of intimidation, fear, discrimination, exclusion and insecurity. This climate limits women’s and girls’ opportunities and freedom and acts as a barrier to their empowerment.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the description of the EDOS label?</strong>",
