    {
      "SurveyID": "SV_9Kzg3KA9F3QnEFM",
      "Element": "SQ",
      "PrimaryAttribute": "QID179",
      "SecondaryAttribute": "faithfulness_card_4327701bda9523e088048486__openai_gpt-6_1-sol",
      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<strong>Paragraph</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">I.B. Awareness-raising measures\n\nI.B.3. Allocate resources to finance effective communication and awareness-raising campaigns on the links between sexism and violence against women and girls, and fund organisations that support victims.\n\nI.B.4. Design, implement and promote regular national awareness-raising initiatives at all levels and through diverse forms of media (for example the production of handbooks, guidelines, video clips available on the internet and in mainstream media, the introduction of a national day against sexism, the setting up of museums to celebrate gender equality and women’s rights). These initiatives should aim to increase awareness and understanding among the general population, especially parents, of different forms of sexism, including phenomena such as “mansplaining”, of how to prevent and respond to them, and of the harm they generate for individuals and society, including girls and boys.</div><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Mansplaining is recognised as a form of sexism to be addressed through public awareness-raising initiatives. These initiatives should increase understanding of how to prevent and respond to such behaviour and of the harm that forms of sexism generate for individuals and society, including girls and boys. Recommended outreach targets the general population, especially parents, through diverse media.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the paragraph?</strong>",
        "DefaultChoices": false,
        "DataExportTag": "faithfulness_card_4327701bda9523e088048486__openai_gpt-6_1-sol",
