        "QuestionText": "<hr><br><strong>EDOS Label</strong><br><p>3.4 condescending explanations or unwelcome advice – Offering unsolicited or patronising advice to women on topics and issues they know more about (known as ‘mansplaining’).</p><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Mansplaining is recognised as a form of sexism to be addressed through public awareness-raising initiatives. These initiatives should increase understanding of how to prevent and respond to such behaviour and of the harm that forms of sexism generate for individuals and society, including girls and boys. Recommended outreach targets the general population, especially parents, through diverse media.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the description of the EDOS label?</strong>",
        "DefaultChoices": false,
