    {
      "SurveyID": "SV_9Kzg3KA9F3QnEFM",
      "Element": "SQ",
      "PrimaryAttribute": "QID187",
      "SecondaryAttribute": "faithfulness_card_e123ca4bf0ea12fcc7888657__deepseek_deepseek-v4_1-flash-1017",
      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<strong>Paragraph</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Appendix to Recommendation CM/Rec(2019)1 &gt; Guidelines for preventing and combating sexism: measures for implementation &gt; Context\n\nSexism and sexist behaviour occur across the full range of human activity, including in cyberspace (internet and social media). They can be experienced individually or collectively by a person or a group of persons, even if neither the individual nor the group has been directly targeted, for example through sexist advertising, or posting of pictures of naked women in the workplace. The three levels of perpetuating and experiencing sexism are: individual, institutional (for example family, work or education environment), and structural (for example through societal gender inequalities, social norms and behaviour). Sexism is silencing when individuals and groups fail to report or complain about sexist behaviour for fear of not being taken seriously, of being ostracised or even held responsible.</div><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Sexism and sexist behaviour occur across all areas of activity, including cyberspace, and can be experienced individually or collectively even when a person or group is not directly targeted. Sexism is perpetuated and experienced at individual, institutional, and structural levels through societal gender inequalities, social norms, and behaviour. Sexism is silencing when individuals and groups do not report or complain about it because they fear not being taken seriously, being ostracised, or being held responsible.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the paragraph?</strong>",
        "DefaultChoices": false,
        "DataExportTag": "faithfulness_card_e123ca4bf0ea12fcc7888657__deepseek_deepseek-v4_1-flash-1017",
        "QuestionType": "MC",
