        "QuestionText": "<hr><br><strong>EDOS Label</strong><br><p>4.2 supporting systemic discrimination against women as a group – Expressing support for systemic discrimination of women as a group. Support can be shown by denying, understating, or seeking to justify such discrimination.</p><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Sexism encompasses any act, gesture, representation, words, practice, or behaviour based on the idea that a person or group is inferior because of sex. It includes acts whose purpose or effect is to create barriers to autonomy and full realisation of human rights or to maintain and reinforce gender stereotypes. Such acts can occur online or offline and in the public or private sphere, and they can violate dignity or rights, cause harm, or create a hostile environment.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the description of the EDOS label?</strong>",
