        "QuestionText": "<hr><br><strong>EDOS Label</strong><br><p>4.2 supporting systemic discrimination against women as a group – Expressing support for systemic discrimination of women as a group. Support can be shown by denying, understating, or seeking to justify such discrimination.</p><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Women are subject to gender discrimination, but they do not all experience it in the same way; their economic, social, political and cultural circumstances can expose them to multiple forms of discrimination. Factors such as race, caste, class, disability, sexual orientation and migration status can shape the nature of violence women and girls suffer and direct discrimination and violence toward particular groups. These intersections can create inequalities unique to some groups or disproportionately affect them, making intersectional discrimination a serious obstacle to gender equality.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the description of the EDOS label?</strong>",
